(a) Application. Application for licenses issued hereunder shall be made upon forms made available by the board of commissioner's office and shall state:
(1) The full name, age, residence, present and previous occupations of the applicant;
(2) A specific description of the location of the principal place of business of the applicant, including proof of ownership, lease or rental;
(3) The number of years of experience the applicant has had as a private detective or in the related fields;
(4) The length of time applicant has been a bona fide resident of the state and county immediately preceding the filing of the application;
(5) Three (3) character references and three (3) business references who have known the applicant for a period of at least three (3) years;
(6) A list of dates and places of employment for five (5) years prior to date of application; and
(7) A photograph and fingerprints made by the police department of the county.
(b) Investigation. Within ten (10) days after receipt of an application as provided for herein, the police committee shall cause an investigation to be made of the applicant and applicant's proposed operation.
